# Netlify HTTP cache headers for the RISE static site.
# Place: this file must ship at the PUBLISH DIRECTORY ROOT. The Netlify mirror
# (universe-rise.netlify.app) publishes verify-web/static/, so it lives here.
# Host coverage: Netlify honors this file. The GitHub Pages mirror ignores it
# (Pages sends its own headers; no per-path config exists there) — HTML pages
# there still revalidate via the service worker's network-first strategy, and
# versioned assets (?v=) are effectively immutable by URL.
# Primary (riseproof.me): apply the same max-age values at that origin.
#
# Convention: site.js / styles.css carry ?v= cache-busters in index.html, so
# they are safe to cache immutably for 1 year. verify.js ships WITHOUT ?v=
# today, so it gets 1 day WITHOUT immutable (fresh verifier logic always wins).
# Stable binaries (video/poster/image/font) are content-hashed by workflow
# (replaced, never edited in place) -> 1 year immutable. HTML -> no-cache.

/site.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/styles.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/verify.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
/*.mp4
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.webm
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.jpg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.jpeg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.webp
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.avif
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.woff2
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.woff
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/assets-real/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
